# Two blue and two black spent (Mox Sapphire x2, Mox Jet x2, Mox Ruby, Mox Emerald): both enters abilities happen. Bot1 names
# `Triggers(reveals; return)`: the first named goes on the stack first, so the return is on top and resolves FIRST. Llanowar Elves is back in
# Bot2's hand (7 cards, checked at the choice) when the hand is revealed, so the nonland choice is between the Elves and the Lightning Bolt
# and Bot1 chooses the Elves: it is discarded, and the Bolt stays. Had the discard resolved first, the Elves could not have been chosen.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Deceit
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Lightning Bolt
Forest x4
Forest x12

[Actions]
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Deceit.Cast
Bot1.Triggers(reveals; return)
Bot1.Target(Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Hand.Count = 7
Bot1.Choose(Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves
Bot2.Hand = Lightning Bolt; Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest
